+## 13. Declared acceptance admission (T-1718)
+
+This closes predicate deletion and fixture-only LIVE closure. VERIFY owns the
+meaning; `acceptance_contract.py` binds the same gate into REVIEW and finish.
+The existing `ticket verify` transaction stores full original/replacement text
+and SHA256 in journal metadata, preserves the old LOG preimage, and binds every
+inspected authority/evidence input to APPLY. A refused mutation writes nothing.
+
+For an outcome amendment, use the existing writer with `--amendment FILE` and
+`--authority SRC-N`. FILE and retained evidence must be owned regular files in
+`.saipen/evidence/`. The closed JSON manifest is:
+
+```json
+{"schema":1,"work":"T-7","original_sha256":"<64hex>",
+ "replacement_sha256":"<64hex>","reason":"why outcomes are equivalent",
+ "evidence":[{"path":".saipen/evidence/retirement.json","sha256":"<64hex>"}],
+ "mapping":{"AC-01":["AC-02"]},"remaining":["AC-02"]}
+```
+
+Every original criterion maps to a nonempty replacement set, with no weaker
+witness floor; remaining lists every new criterion. Current sufficient
+replacement evidence is required before application. Removing all outcomes or
+declaring them optional without equivalent proof is refused. Human equivalence
+judgment belongs to the explicit approval, never natural-language inference.
+The operator's exact Source body approves the manifest's complete SHA256:
+
+```json
+{"schema":1,"kind":"acceptance_amendment","work":"T-7","sha256":"<64hex>"}
+```
+
+Approval must be an ACTIVE `user_instruction` Source with immutable verified
+operator-carrier provenance. Capturing model text grants nothing. Later CLOSED
+archival approval remains checkable against original bytes; retired, changed,
+missing, foreign or stale approval refuses. Replay cannot spend an earlier
+contract's approval on the current contract. Duplicate/unknown fields refuse.
+
+LIVE/MANUAL evidence uses the existing anchored RUN record, for example:
+
+```text
+AC-EVIDENCE AC-02 PASS manual witness=LIVE surface=chatgpt.com source=SRC-9 -- observed outcome
+```
+
+Its operator observation Source has this closed body:
+
+```json
+{"schema":1,"kind":"acceptance_witness","work":"T-7",
+ "contract_sha256":"<64hex>","build_event":123,
+ "criteria":{"AC-02":{"result":"PASS","witness":"LIVE","surface":"chatgpt.com"}}}
+```
+
+The digest covers the complete canonical verify field. Journaled note-only
+changes may retain a prior observation when every parsed criterion text and
+witness specification is identical; unknown digests grant nothing.
+`build_event` is the
+latest native BUILD event for that Work, or zero when no BUILD event exists.
+The authenticated report must match the claimed criterion/result/witness/
+surface. This is human-reported scope, not automated observation. The native
+reader checks receipt integrity before selection; re-entering BUILD, changing
+the contract or tampering with retained bytes invalidates earlier evidence.
+Legacy untyped Work is explicitly unaffected, and proves no historical LIVE
+outcome by this new gate.
