+### Declared acceptance preservation (`SRC-216`)
+
+Deleting a failing predicate cannot earn PASS. Native REVIEW and atomic finish
+both enforce declared `AC-NN [WITNESS] outcome` criteria through
+`acceptance_contract`; an ordinary verification PASS does not replace them.
+Legacy untyped clauses retain legacy semantics, never retrospective LIVE proof.
+`ticket verify` preserves before/replacement text and SHA256 in its existing
+journal. Outcome deletion, redefinition or witness reduction needs the exact
+operator-approved amendment described in OPS §13. Every original outcome must
+map to an independently evidenced replacement at the same or stronger floor.
+Implementation changes preserving outcomes need no amendment.
+
+An `AC-EVIDENCE` LIVE/MANUAL label alone grants no observed product scope.
+`source=SRC-N` binds an immutable operator-carrier observation to Work, complete
+contract digest, latest BUILD event, criterion, result, witness and surface.
+It proves what the human reported, not an automatic browser measurement.
+Model-supplied ingress and a stronger retry environment cannot authenticate it.
+Missing/weak/stale/contested evidence refuses with no canonical writes. Typed
+Work supersession additionally preserves equivalent independently satisfied
+successor criteria and requires actual operator provenance; its existing
+dedicated authority and completion gates remain due.
